</section> <section id="flavour" class="wt-section wt-flavour">
  <h3 class="wt-flavour__heading">Pick a flavour</h3>
  <div class="wt-flavour__grid">
    <a href="{{ p_sushi.url | default: knead_collection_url }}" class="wt-flavour__card"><div class="wt-flavour__media">{% if p_sushi.featured_image %}<img src="{{ p_sushi.featured_image | image_url: width: 700 }}" width="{{ p_sushi.featured_image.width }}" height="{{ p_sushi.featured_image.height }}" alt="{{ p_sushi.title }}" class="wt-flavour__img">{% endif %}</div><div class="wt-flavour__row"><span class="wt-flavour__name">Knead That Sushi &mdash; Season 2</span><span class="wt-flavour__price">{{ p_sushi.price | money_without_trailing_zeros | default: '$20' }}</span></div><span class="wt-flavour__meta">9 styles &middot; 1 rare</span></a>
    <div class="wt-flavour__card"><div class="wt-flavour__media">{% render 'wt-img', img: section.settings.ice_image, label: 'Ice cream art', fit: 'contain' %}<span class="wt-flavour__badge">Sept 15</span></div><div class="wt-flavour__row"><span class="wt-flavour__name">Knead That Ice Cream</span><span class="wt-flavour__price">$20</span></div><span class="wt-flavour__meta">Coming soon</span></div>
    <div class="wt-flavour__card"><div class="wt-flavour__media">{% render 'wt-img', img: section.settings.burger_image, label: 'Burger art', fit: 'contain' %}<span class="wt-flavour__badge">Oct 15</span></div><div class="wt-flavour__row"><span class="wt-flavour__name">Knead That Burger</span><span class="wt-flavour__price">$20</span></div><span class="wt-flavour__meta">Coming soon</span></div>
  </div>
</section> {%- comment -%}
  Sushi Blocks (SKU 565) and Ice Cream Blocks (SKU 568): the same
  kinetic fidget in two foods, at two SKUs, sharing one heading and
  sitting side by side.

  They had a full-width band each and read as the same thing said
  twice. The pair now uses the shape #bubble already uses for two
  related products -- a head, then a two-column grid of cards --
  rather than the wide wt-new card, which is built to carry one
  product across the page and does not halve. Each card still keeps
  its own photo, price and button, because these are two things a
  visitor buys separately.

  Three guards, not one. The band appears if either product does, and
  each card appears only with its own product, so a flavour that is
  not on the Online Store channel drops out and leaves the other
  standing rather than taking the heading down with it.
{%- endcomment -%}
