</section> <section id="tagd" class="wt-section wt-tagd">
  {% assign tagd_col = collections['tagd'] %}
  <div class="wt-tagd__grid">
    <div>
      <p class="wt-tagd__eyebrow">Works with Apple AirTag</p>
      <h2 class="wt-tagd__title">tag'd 2</h2>
      <p class="wt-tagd__body">A slap watch with a pocket for an AirTag, so you can find it on the bus, at school, or wherever it ended up. Kids set the time themselves. AirTag sold separately.</p>
      <div class="wt-tagd__steps">
        <div class="wt-tagd__step"><span class="wt-tagd__step-num">1</span><span class="wt-tagd__step-text">Drop an AirTag into the pocket on the band.</span></div>
        <div class="wt-tagd__step"><span class="wt-tagd__step-num">2</span><span class="wt-tagd__step-text">Slap it on. One size, no buckles, no help needed.</span></div>
        <div class="wt-tagd__step"><span class="wt-tagd__step-num wt-tagd__step-num--accent">3</span><span class="wt-tagd__step-text">Find it in the Find My app when it goes missing.</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="wt-tagd__actions">
        <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/tagd" class="wt-btn">Shop Tag'd &mdash; {{ p_tagd.price | money_without_trailing_zeros | default: '$30' }}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    {%- comment -%}
      The same nine photos the row below is built from, stacked and
      cross-faded, so hovering a style in the row shows it here at size.
      Requested at width 900 rather than the 1200 the single photo used:
      that is the width the hero asks for, so the nine URLs are the nine
      the hero already fetched and the band adds no download at all.

      alt="" for the same reason the hero's are empty -- the row below is
      nine links that each carry the style's name in both text and alt,
      so naming them again here would read the collection out twice.

      The scale corrections come with them. Cover crops rather than fits,
      but it does not change that the watch is shot at nine sizes, and a
      swap that lands on a different-sized watch is exactly the jump the
      hero was fixed for -- more visible here, at this size.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="wt-tagd__media">{% if tagd_col.products.size > 0 %}{% for product in tagd_col.products limit: 9 %}{%- assign tagd_scale = '1' -%}{%- for pair in tagd_scales -%}{%- assign kv = pair | split: ':' -%}{%- if kv[0] == product.handle -%}{%- assign tagd_scale = kv[1] -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}<img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 900 }}" width="{{ product.featured_image.width }}" height="{{ product.featured_image.height }}" alt="" class="wt-tagd__img wt-tagd__img--switch wt-tagd__img--{{ forloop.index0 }}"{% unless tagd_scale == '1' %} style="transform: scale({{ tagd_scale }})"{% endunless %}>{% endfor %}{% elsif p_tagd.featured_image %}<img src="{{ p_tagd.featured_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}" width="{{ p_tagd.featured_image.width }}" height="{{ p_tagd.featured_image.height }}" alt="{{ p_tagd.title }}" class="wt-tagd__img">{% endif %}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="wt-tagd__row">
    {% for product in tagd_col.products limit: 9 %}
    <a href="{{ product.url }}" class="wt-tagd__card"><div class="wt-tagd__card-media"><img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 500 }}" width="{{ product.featured_image.width }}" height="{{ product.featured_image.height }}" alt="{{ product.title }}" class="wt-tagd__card-img"></div><span class="wt-tagd__card-name">{{ product.title | split: ' - ' | first }}</span></a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
